#!/bin/bash
export QWEN_DEADLINE=1200
python3 ~/.claude/bin/qwen_agent.py "RESEARCH TASK (web search; cite URLs; only state facts you found). I need a FREE, open-licence (Apache/MIT/BSD or clearly allowing commercial use), fully LOCAL text-to-speech model that runs on an Apple Silicon Mac (M5 Max, 64 GB, macOS, Python 3.12-3.14 via uv) for a warm, gentle, female, children's-storybook read-aloud narrator in English (a 60-90 second trailer, and later longer). Compare at least: Kokoro-82M (mlx-audio or kokoro-onnx), Chatterbox (Resemble), Piper, Qwen3-TTS, Orpheus, Dia, F5-TTS, Parler-TTS, Sesame CSM, and anything newer you find in 2026. For each give: licence (and of the weights), size, whether it runs on Mac GPU (MLX/MPS) or CPU, expected naturalness for storytelling, whether it can control pace/emotion, and the exact install and one-line run command. Recommend the top 2 and say which voice names to try. Output a concise markdown report ending with a RECOMMENDATION section." > tts_report.md 2> tts_err.log
python3 ~/.claude/bin/qwen_agent.py "RESEARCH TASK (web search; cite URLs; only state facts you found). I need to keep cartoon/watercolor storybook characters visually consistent across many images using FREE local tools on a Mac with the Draw Things CLI (draw-things-cli generate/train lora) and models Z-Image Turbo, FLUX.2 klein (4B/9B), Qwen-Image-Edit-2511, Qwen-Image. Find out: (1) how to train a small character LoRA with draw-things-cli train lora (dataset size, captions, steps, rank, learning rate, resolution, time on Apple Silicon) and best practice for 4 separate characters; can a LoRA trained on Z-Image Base or FLUX.2 klein be used at generation time via generate --config-json loras? (2) Does Draw Things support reference-image / multi-reference editing with FLUX.2 klein or Qwen-Image-Edit-2511 (how many reference images, how to pass them from the CLI or API)? (3) Practical tips for consistent characters in painterly styles (trigger words, caption style, mixing two character LoRAs in one image, LoRA strength). Output a concise markdown report with sources and a RECOMMENDATION section (which method first, which second, which to avoid)." > consistency_report.md 2> consistency_err.log
python3 ~/.claude/bin/qwen_agent.py "RESEARCH TASK (web search; cite URLs; only state facts you found). For image-to-video with LTX-2.3 (Lightricks, distilled 22B, run through Draw Things on a Mac) animating a PAINTED / watercolor children's-book illustration that contains people and a dragon: find prompting and settings tips to keep faces and hands stable and avoid morphing, keep the painterly texture (no photoreal drift), keep camera still or do a slow push-in, and get subtle secondary motion (mist, leaves, hair, cloth). Also find recommended frame counts/resolution/steps/cfg, and any known problems with 2D or watercolor art. Output a concise markdown report with sources and a RECOMMENDATION section with an example prompt template." > ltx_report.md 2> ltx_err.log
echo DONE > research_done.flag
